-- title:
--   Non-normic split classes: vanishing of the weighted window combination
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L$ a finite Galois extension of $K$, $\sigma$ is an element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every element of the Galois group lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (`hgen`), and $\ell := [L:K]$ (`Module.finrank K L`) is assumed prime (`hprime`). A Haar measure `νZK` is fixed on the group $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ of ideles, and $S_K$, $T$ are finite sets of finite places of $K$ with $T$ disjoint from $S_K$ (`hTS`). For a unit $u\in K^\times$ and an idele $z$, write $\gamma_{u,z} := c(z)\,\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$ for the product of the central scalar matrix attached to $z$ with the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$, $u$ being transported to the ideles by the map induced by $K\to\mathbb{A}_K$.
--
--   *Test data and matching.* The function $f_\infty :=$ `faK` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ is an archimedean test factor (`hfaK`: it is a compactly supported function given by a smooth function of the matrix entries in the mixed space), the functions `fSK v` for $v\in S_K$ are locally constant with compact support (`hfSK`), `φa` is an archimedean test factor for $L$ (`hφa`), and for $v\in S_K$ the functions `φS v` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ are locally constant with compact support (`hφS`). The hypotheses `hmatchA` and `hmatchS` assert matching in the sense of `AreMatchingOn`, at the archimedean place for the pair $(\mathtt{φa}\circ\mathtt{archIdentGL},\,f_\infty)$ with respect to the Haar measures `archHaarL`, `archHaarK`, and at each $v\in S_K$ for the pair $(\mathtt{φS}\,v,\mathtt{fSK}\,v)$ with respect to `semiLocalHaar` and `localHaar`: twisted orbital integrals of the $L$-side function at $\delta$ agree with orbital integrals of the $K$-side function at $\gamma$ whenever the norm string $\delta\,\sigma(\delta)\cdots\sigma^{\ell-1}(\delta)$ and $\gamma$ are regular semisimple, some $y$ conjugates the norm string to the image of $\gamma$, and the Haar measures on the ($\sigma$-twisted) centralisers are coupled; and orbital integrals of the $K$-side function vanish at regular semisimple $\gamma$ admitting no norm. The functions `fT v`, $v\in T$, are locally constant with compact support (`hfT`) and each admits a locally constant compactly supported semi-local partner matching it in the same sense (`hmatchT`). Outside $S_K\cup T$ the unit hypothesis `hunit` asserts that the indicator of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` matches the indicator of `localIntegralSet K v`.
--
--   *Global factorisation.* The functions $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ and `ff` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\mathrm{fin}})$ satisfy `hf`, the predicate `IsUnitFactorization` for the set $S_K\cup T$ with local data $v\mapsto \mathtt{fT}\,v$ for $v\in T$ and $v\mapsto\mathtt{fSK}\,v$ otherwise: $f_\infty$ is an archimedean test factor, `ff` is locally constant with compact support, the chosen local functions are local test functions on $S_K\cup T$, `ff` is the product of those local functions at the components in $S_K\cup T$ whenever all components outside $S_K\cup T$ lie in `localIntegralSet`, `ff` vanishes when some component outside $S_K\cup T$ does not, and $f(g)=f_\infty(g_\infty)\,\mathtt{ff}(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$ for all $g$.
--
--   *Measure factorisation constants.* A measure `νA` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ and a real constant $c_G$ are given such that `hG` holds: for every finite set $S$, every factorisable datum $(f,f_\infty,f_S)$ satisfying the stated measurability conditions, the product formula at components in $S$ and the vanishing condition outside $S$, the integral of $f$ against `adelicGLHaar` equals $c_G\,(\int f_\infty\,d\mathtt{νA})\prod_{v\in S}\int \mathtt{fS}\,v\,d\mathtt{localHaar}$. A constant $c_{\tau K}>0$ (`hcτK`) and measures `τG u z` on the centraliser of $\gamma_{u,z}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ are given which are Haar for $u\neq 1$ (`hτG`) and for which `hτGc` expresses every integral over the centraliser as $c_{\tau K}$ times the integral over $(\mathbb{A}_K^\times)^2$ of the corresponding diagonal matrices against `νZK.prod νZK`. Likewise measures `τA u z` on the centraliser of the archimedean component of $\gamma_{u,z}$ and `τF u z v` on the local centralisers are Haar for $u\neq 1$ (`hτA`, `hτF`), the local ones being normalised so that the preimage of `localIntegralSet K v` has mass $1$ (`hτF1`); and a constant $c_T>0$ (`hcT`) satisfies `hT`: for $u\neq 1$ and factorisable data on the centraliser with the stated measurability and vanishing conditions, $\int W\,d\mathtt{τG} = c_T\,(\int W_\infty\,d\mathtt{τA})\prod_{v\in S}\int W_v\,d\mathtt{τF}$.
--
--   *Windows on the $K$-side.* For $u\neq 1$, `IA u z` is an orbital integral of $f_\infty$ at the archimedean component of $\gamma_{u,z}$ with respect to `νA` and `τA u z` (`hIA`), and `IF u z v` an orbital integral of `fSK v` at the $v$-component for $v\in S_K$ (`hIF`); here an orbital integral is given by a non-negative measurable compactly supported section function whose integral over the centraliser translates equals $1$ on the support of the conjugated test function. Similarly `JA u z` is a weighted orbital integral of $f_\infty$ with weight $y\mapsto -\log\mathtt{archHeight}_K(y)-\log\mathtt{archHeight}_K(w_\infty y)$, $w$ being the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ of $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ (`hJA`), and `JF u z v` a weighted orbital integral of `fSK v` with the local weight, for $v\in S_K$ (`hJF`).
--
--   *Twisted side.* A measure `νA'` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ is given, together with the normalisations `hνA`: $\mathtt{νA}=\mathtt{archHaarK}\,K$ and `hνA'`: $\mathtt{νA'}=\mathtt{archHaarL}\,K\,L$. Elements `δA u z` are chosen so that, whenever the archimedean component of $\gamma_{u,z}$ admits a norm, the norm string of `δA u z` equals the image of that component under `toTensorGL` (`hδA`), i.e. `δA u z` is a norm of it with conjugator $1$; the measures `τA' u z` on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $\{t : t\,\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1}=\delta\}$ of `δA u z` are Haar (`hτA'`) and, in the presence of a norm, coupled to `τA u z` with conjugator $1$ (`hτA'c`), i.e. the pushforward of `τA' u z` along conjugation by $1$ equals the pushforward of `τA u z` along `toTensorGL`. Analogously `δF u z v` satisfies the norm-string identity at $v\in S_K$ (`hδF`), and `τF' u z v` are Haar (`hτF'`) with the preimage of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` of mass $1$ (`hτF'1`). The quantity `JA' u z` is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\mathtt{φa}\circ\mathtt{archIdentGL}$ at `δA u z` with respect to `νA'`, `τA' u z` and the weight $y\mapsto -\log\mathtt{archHeight}_L(\mathtt{archIdentGL}\,y)-\log\mathtt{archHeight}_L(w_{L,\infty}\,\mathtt{archIdentGL}\,y)$ whenever a norm exists (`hJA'`), and vanishes when none does (`hJA'0`); likewise `JF' u z v`, for $v\in S_K$, is a twisted weighted orbital integral of `φS v` at `δF u z v` with the semi-local weight when a norm exists (`hJF'`) and vanishes otherwise (`hJF'0`).
--
--   *Hecke and unit windows.* For $u\neq 1$, `IT u z v` is an orbital integral of `fT v` at the $v$-component of $\gamma_{u,z}$ for $v\in T$ (`hIT`), and `IU u z v` an orbital integral of the indicator of `localIntegralSet K v` for $v\notin S_K\cup T$ (`hIU`).
--
--   *The class.* An element $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ is diagonal with non-trivial ratio: its $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries vanish and $\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11}\neq 1$ (`hγ`); units $u_\gamma,d_\gamma\in K^\times$ satisfy $u_\gamma=\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11}$ (`huγ`) and $d_\gamma=\gamma_{11}$ (`hdγ`). The hypothesis `hγnn` is that $u_\gamma$ does not lie in the range of the norm map $\mathrm{N}_{L/K}:L\to K$. A Haar measure `τK` is fixed on the centraliser of the image of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ (`hτK`), satisfying the same reduction to $(\mathbb{A}_K^\times)^2$ with constant $c_{\tau K}$ (`hτKc`). Real constants $c_G'$, $c_T'$ are given, with $c_G>0$, $c_G'>0$, $c_T'>0$ (`hcG`, `hcG'`, `hcT'`). Finally an idele $z$ is fixed and $J\in\mathbb{C}$ is a weighted orbital integral, with respect to `adelicGLHaar` and `τK`, of the function $g\mapsto f(c(z)g)$ at the image of $\gamma$, for the weight $x\mapsto -\log h_{\mathbb{A}}(x)-\log h_{\mathbb{A}}(wx)$ with $h_{\mathbb{A}}$ the adelic height and $w$ the adelic Weyl element (`hJ`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses, writing $z_\gamma := z\cdot d_\gamma$ for the product of $z$ with the image of $d_\gamma$ in the ideles, the following identity in $\mathbb{C}$ holds:
--   $$\ell\cdot\frac{c_G'c_T}{c_Gc_T'}\cdot J\;+\;\frac{c_G'}{c_T'}\Big(\prod_{v\in T} I_T(u_\gamma,z_\gamma,v)\Big)\Big(\textstyle\prod^{\mathrm f}_{v\notin S_K\cup T} I_U(u_\gamma,z_\gamma,v)\Big)\Big[\big(J_A'(u_\gamma,z_\gamma)-\ell\,J_A(u_\gamma,z_\gamma)\big)\prod_{v\in S_K} I_F(u_\gamma,z_\gamma,v)\;+\;I_A(u_\gamma,z_\gamma)\sum_{v\in S_K}\big(J_F'(u_\gamma,z_\gamma,v)-\ell\,J_F(u_\gamma,z_\gamma,v)\big)\prod_{v'\in S_K\setminus\{v\}} I_F(u_\gamma,z_\gamma,v')\Big]\;=\;0,$$
--   where the two scalar factors $(c_G'c_T)/(c_Gc_T')$ and $c_G'c_T'^{-1}$ are formed in $\mathbb{R}$ and then viewed in $\mathbb{C}$, $\ell$ denotes the image of $[L:K]$ in $\mathbb{C}$, the second product is the finitely supported product (`∏ᶠ`) over all finite places $v$ of $K$ subject to $v\notin S_K\cup T$, and the inner products over $S_K\setminus\{v\}$ are over `SK.erase v`.
--
--   This is the per-class cancellation identity on the hyperbolic side of the comparison of weighted (non-invariant) trace formulae for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$ along a cyclic extension of prime degree: at a diagonal rational class whose ratio is not a global norm from $L$, the weighted global class term, rescaled by the measure constants, cancels against the bracket built from the archimedean and local windows and their twisted counterparts. It is used in the assembly of the winding-datum identity [`AutomorphicForm.exists_const_forall_exists_windingDatum_hyperbolicIntercept_sub_finrank_mul_const_mul_sum_eq_sum_satakeLaurent_mul_coeff_of_eq_affine_of_areMatchingArch_of_areMatchingLocal`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_const_forall_exists_windingDatum_hyperbolicIntercept_sub_finrank_mul_const_mul_sum_eq_sum_satakeLaurent_mul_coeff_of_eq_affine_of_areMatchingArch_of_areMatchingLocal), and rests on the existence of a set of places at which the local class admits no norm together with the algebraic cancellation lemma [`AutomorphicForm.finrank_mul_ratio_mul_add_mul_window_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_eq_zero_of_not_singleton`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.finrank_mul_ratio_mul_add_mul_window_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_eq_zero_of_not_singleton).
